            <ArticleTitle>Obesity: cerebral damage in obesity-associated metabolic syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>642-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1038/nrendo.2014.141</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The prevalence of the metabolic syndrome has increased in tandem with that of obesity. The metabolic syndrome is associated with structural and functional cerebral damage. A new study confirms the association between the metabolic syndrome and reduced brain volume in the absence of diabetes mellitus. Here, we highlight how vascular dysfunction potentially contributes to this brain damage.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
